# ThreadSanitizer suppressions — each entry documents a DELIBERATE
# benign race; anything not listed here fails the tsan-gate.
#
# The deadlock watchdog is a warn-only, lock-free, best-effort scanner
# BY DESIGN (see watchdog_thread_fn's header comment): it reads process
# slab fields and io port counts without synchronization, tolerating
# torn/stale values, because a false positive only mistimes a warning.
# Making those fields _Atomic is a Phase-2.4 decision (sw_process.state
# is written on every context switch — hot path). Until then: suppress
# the scanner, not the runtime.
race:watchdog_thread_fn
race:sw_io_active_port_count
